    "body": "Use the DiagnosticDeprecated hlgroup to differentiate between deprecated vs normal items in the completion menu.\r\n\r\nTook \"inspiration\" from here https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua#L320\r\n\r\nbefore:\r\n<img width=\"422\" height=\"273\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6edf288d-4c88-4d41-854f-70d87559ce9a\" />\r\n\r\nafter:\r\n<img width=\"433\" height=\"280\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/26ef1cfb-9a3e-42ca-b207-232a00a45d8d\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-09-23T11:53:37Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nThe `abbr_hlgroup` functionality is only available in Neovim>=0.11, while 'mini.nvim' currently supports Neovim>=0.9. So this will require a bit more care on top of improving performance of the if-else check.\r\n\r\nBut the main reason of why this was not yet added is that I don't particularly like this functionality and find it distracting. Maybe it can be added behind a dedicated 'MiniCompletionXxx' highlight group, not sure.\r\n\r\nFor future, I'd highly appreciate if issue is created first to discuss this (as described in 'CONTRIBUTING.md').",
